&lt;p&gt;Union Parliamentary Affairs Minister Kiren Rijiju on Saturday launched a fresh attack on Congress leader Rahul Gandhi, challenging him to answer four questions concerning India's history, the 1962 war with China and the country's economic record. Rijiju, who belongs to Arunachal Pradesh, invoked his personal connection to the 1962 conflict, alleging that his village had been occupied by China. He also accused the Congress of failing to address India's economic challenges during its years in power.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In a post on X, the minister posed four questions to the opposition party: &quot;My village was occupied by China in 1962. Will Congress apologize for 1962 humiliation?&quot;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&quot;Congress kept India a poor nation. Why?. Why was India called land of snake charmers?. Why was India's economy insulted as Hindu rate of growth?,&quot; he said.&lt;/p&gt;
