&lt;p&gt;US President Donald Trump has voiced support for Jensen Huang's possible return to Nvidia, saying the former chief executive deserves another opportunity despite the controversy surrounding his exit from the chipmaker. Trump described Huang as one of the world's brightest minds and urged him to apologise before returning to the company he co-founded.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Speaking to reporters on Friday, Trump expressed his willingness to see Huang resume leadership at Nvidia, which plays a crucial role in the global artificial intelligence industry. &quot;I think that I would love to see Jensen be given a second chance,&quot; Trump said. Describing Huang as &quot;a good man&quot; who &quot;made some bad decisions&quot;, Trump added that he wanted the former CEO to issue an apology and return to the company.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&quot;I'd like to see Jensen make a big apology and go back because he created something with Blackwell,&quot; he said, referring to Nvidia's advanced chip architecture.&lt;/p&gt;
